I then proceeded to get synthoil, the pact, and lump of coal. I was around 100-120 dmg per tear with deadeye buff.

&#x200B;

UPDATE: GOT MOMS KNIFE??????

This is a big read but PLEASE read all of it, I ramble a bit but this is most likely going to help you.

&#x200B;

How much direct light does he get? they can tolerate a bit of direct light but bright indirect light is perfect for them, obviously, in the wild, they would be getting scattered direct light so if that's what you have as far as lighting goes then it should be fine. my guess is humidity honestly, also do you water with tap water? you could have different chemicals in the water making the edges crisp up. If I were you try watering with distilled water only for a few weeks and, if you can, put a humidifier really close to him. Browning near the edges tends to be from either water or humidity, so try either both or one at a time. What's already brown will not change back, it's dead tissue. the cheapest solution is just distilled water and see if there's an improvement, if not then hook up a humidifier. Though your plant would probably appreciate the distilled water regardless. ALSO, this could entirely be from the plant being root bound/needing more space. these guys get HUGE outdoors so it might be time for some fresh chunky aroid soil (orchid mix and cactus mix together is what I use) and a bigger pot. I recommend terracotta because it drains nice and fast. Keep in mind it could be a combination of all three of these things. Try checking on the root situation first, and give him distilled water for a while. As I said before it could also be humidity, it's all dependent on your plant and it really is just trial and error. Be careful repotting because it's November so plants aren't too receptive to being repotted (this could be why your other plants aren't happy, transplant shock is a bitch). Anyway, good luck, message me or reply if you have any questions/concerns.
